WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.933 --> 00:00:17.893
Hey, so how much more
we got left to load?

2
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.560
Uh, just this last row.

3
00:00:19.729 --> 00:00:22.449
The sooner we finish,
the sooner this truck gets to Cleveland.

4
00:00:22.565 --> 00:00:24.865
Watch the turn.
Watch what? Ow!

5
00:00:25.026 --> 00:00:27.866
Too late.
Okay, I think we're close. Whee!

6
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:31.205
Hi!

7
00:00:31.324 --> 00:00:32.454
Is this quarantine?

8
00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:34.413
Yes! This is it!
We're in quarantine!

9
00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:36.997
My parents are here!

10
00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:38.390
Where are we going?
Hey, what...

11
00:00:38.414 --> 00:00:39.725
No, why are we going towards the door?

12
00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:41.959
- We are all better!
- Yay!

13
00:00:42.043 --> 00:00:43.753
I feel fantastic!

14
00:00:45.421 --> 00:00:46.421
Dude.

15
00:00:48.591 --> 00:00:51.801
My family! Come on, let's go!
Excuse me.

16
00:00:51.886 --> 00:00:53.056
Dory, wait a minute!

17
00:00:56.641 --> 00:01:00.271
I'm coming Mommy! I'm coming Daddy!

18
00:01:01.229 --> 00:01:04.269
Whoo-hoo! Almost home.
Almost home. I'm almost home.

19
00:01:04.398 --> 00:01:07.068
I think I'm getting
the hang of this! Oh!

20
00:01:10.905 --> 00:01:12.365
I hear footsteps.

21
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:16.494
- Hank!
- Quiet.

22
00:01:16.744 --> 00:01:19.124
Hank, we need to get in that tank.
That rhymed.

23
00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:21.128
- Why?
- Her parents are there!

24
00:01:21.499 --> 00:01:22.579
Oh.

25
00:01:22.667 --> 00:01:26.637
Look, you've got three minutes
to get everyone in this cup with you...

26
00:01:26.796 --> 00:01:28.676
and then I'm on that truck
to Cleveland, got it?

27
00:01:28.798 --> 00:01:29.798
Got it.

28
00:01:34.178 --> 00:01:35.438
Oh boy.

29
00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:41.602
Mom? Dad?

30
00:01:41.769 --> 00:01:46.099
Mom? Dad?
Hey, everybody. It's me, Dory!

31
00:01:47.316 --> 00:01:49.826
Dory? Dory? Dory?
Jenny and Charlie's Dory? Dory?

32
00:01:49.944 --> 00:01:51.654
Mom? Dad?

33
00:01:52.488 --> 00:01:53.998
Mom? Dad?

34
00:01:55.324 --> 00:01:57.284
Mom? Dad?

35
00:01:58.202 --> 00:02:00.832
- She should just pick 2 and let's go.
- Dad.

36
00:02:00.997 --> 00:02:03.417
What? I'm kidding. It's a reunion.

37
00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:07.331
Mom? Dad? Where are my parents?

38
00:02:08.337 --> 00:02:11.427
Dory? Are you really
Jenny and Charlie's girl?

39
00:02:11.549 --> 00:02:14.509
Yes, I am! That's me! Where are they?

40
00:02:14.635 --> 00:02:17.845
Uh, well, Dory, right after
you disappeared, they thought you...

41
00:02:18.014 --> 00:02:21.354
Well, they thought you must have
ended up here, in quarantine.

42
00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.354
- Uh-huh?
- Come on, come on, come on.

43
00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:28.028
And so they came here to look for you.

44
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.860
They're here! Where are they?

45
00:02:32.153 --> 00:02:35.693
Dory, that was years ago.

46
00:02:35.865 --> 00:02:38.705
- Huh?
- They never came back.

47
00:02:38.826 --> 00:02:39.956
Oh no.

48
00:02:40.077 --> 00:02:44.457
You see, Dory, when fish
don't come back from quarantine...

49
00:02:44.582 --> 00:02:46.792
it means they're not...

50
00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:48.501
What?

51
00:02:49.045 --> 00:02:51.255
Dory, they're gone.

52
00:02:51.339 --> 00:02:53.709
They're dead?

53
00:02:54.467 --> 00:02:58.057
- They wanted to find you...
- Wait. Are you sure they're gone?

54
00:02:58.888 --> 00:03:01.018
Dory, listen, it's going to be okay.

55
00:03:01.182 --> 00:03:02.552
Dory, they loved you so much.

56
00:03:02.725 --> 00:03:05.565
Anyone not looking to go to Cleveland,
final warning!

57
00:03:08.272 --> 00:03:11.102
- Dory, are you all right?
- Are you okay?

58
00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:14.403
- I was too late.
- Dory, no. No. Now listen.

59
00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:18.400
- I don't have a family.
- No, Dory. That's not true.

60
00:03:19.075 --> 00:03:21.285
Time to go!

61
00:03:21.452 --> 00:03:23.282
I'm all alone.

62
00:03:23.454 --> 00:03:24.954
Dory.
Dory!

63
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:28.628
Where's everybody else?

64
00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:32.085
Your orange friends are on their way
to Cleveland. Ah!

65
00:03:32.254 --> 00:03:33.924
I found the octopus!

66
00:03:35.216 --> 00:03:36.856
Where did he go?

67
00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:47.397
Mommy? Daddy?

68
00:03:53.943 --> 00:03:54.943
Help.

69
00:03:56.779 --> 00:04:01.279
No. No. No. Help. Help. Help me.

70
00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:06.790
Help. Help me. Please.
Somebody help me!

71
00:04:08.124 --> 00:04:10.504
Hey, can... Help me?
Can you help me? I've lost them!

72
00:04:10.668 --> 00:04:14.008
- Oh. Lost who?
- I-I-I-I...

73
00:04:14.171 --> 00:04:17.001
Ah, sorry, honey. I can't help you
if you don't remember.

74
00:04:17.633 --> 00:04:19.263
Uh...

75
00:04:20.428 --> 00:04:23.518
Oh! Can you help me? I've lost... them.

76
00:04:23.681 --> 00:04:25.011
Uh, can you be more specific?

77
00:04:25.182 --> 00:04:27.432
My... My... Them! Them! Them!

78
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.640
Um... Um...

79
00:04:31.647 --> 00:04:32.647
Oh...

80
00:04:33.983 --> 00:04:36.313
Help! Help!

81
00:04:37.820 --> 00:04:40.440
Please? They're gone!

82
00:04:54.795 --> 00:04:59.635
I've lost... I've lost everyone.
There's nothing I can do.

83
00:05:01.719 --> 00:05:06.009
Shoot, I can't forget.
What was I forgetting? Something.

84
00:05:07.349 --> 00:05:09.889
Something important. What was it? I...

85
00:05:11.687 --> 00:05:15.027
What was it? It's going away.

86
00:05:15.858 --> 00:05:19.868
It's going away. It's going because
all I can do is forget. I just forget.

87
00:05:20.029 --> 00:05:24.149
And I forget.
That's what I do best. That's what I do.

88
00:05:25.493 --> 00:05:30.043
What do I do? What do I do?
What do I do? What do I do?

89
00:05:32.041 --> 00:05:33.711
What would Dory do?

90
00:05:36.378 --> 00:05:38.218
I would look around.

91
00:05:40.716 --> 00:05:44.556
And, um, there's just water over there.
And a lot of kelp over here.

92
00:05:45.554 --> 00:05:47.224
Kelp is better. Okay.

93
00:05:52.937 --> 00:05:57.527
Okay. Now what? Lots of kelp.
It looks the same.

94
00:05:58.859 --> 00:06:03.239
It all looks the same,
except there's a rock... over there.

95
00:06:03.906 --> 00:06:08.876
And some sand this way.
I like sand. Sand is squishy.

96
00:06:24.593 --> 00:06:26.093
Oh this isn't going anywhere.

97
00:06:28.222 --> 00:06:33.312
There's nothing here.
Nothing but kelp. Lots of kelp.

98
00:06:33.477 --> 00:06:37.607
And some shells... this way.

99
00:06:38.941 --> 00:06:40.271
I like shells.

100
00:06:43.821 --> 00:06:47.241
I like... shells.

101
00:07:13.601 --> 00:07:14.931
Whoa.

102
00:07:52.389 --> 00:07:53.969
Hello. I'm...

103
00:07:54.099 --> 00:07:57.389
- Dory!
- Dory! You're here.

104
00:07:57.561 --> 00:07:59.311
- Oh my baby!
- You're really here.

105
00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:00.665
- Let me look at you.
- You found us.

106
00:08:00.689 --> 00:08:02.959
- I'm never letting you go again.
- Oh my missing girl, you're here.

107
00:08:02.983 --> 00:08:04.023
- My baby!
- It's you.

108
00:08:04.193 --> 00:08:07.863
- Yes! Oh absolutely!
- It's really you! Mom, you're here.

109
00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:10.700
- I am, I...
- And Dad, so are you.

110
00:08:10.783 --> 00:08:12.323
Right here, kelpcake.

111
00:08:15.871 --> 00:08:17.541
I'm so sorry.

112
00:08:17.706 --> 00:08:20.376
Oh honey. Oh honey, no. Kelpcake.

113
00:08:20.542 --> 00:08:24.212
I know I've got a problem. I know I'm...
And I'm so sorry.

114
00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:28.460
And all this time I've wanted to fix it
and I can't and I try. I try.

115
00:08:28.550 --> 00:08:31.380
But my thoughts... they leave my head
and ideas change.

116
00:08:31.553 --> 00:08:33.683
And I'd forgotten you and I'm so sorry.

117
00:08:33.847 --> 00:08:38.897
Dory. Don't you dare be sorry.
Look what you did.

118
00:08:39.561 --> 00:08:42.731
- What?
- You found us!

119
00:08:42.898 --> 00:08:44.658
That's right. You found us.

120
00:08:46.151 --> 00:08:49.611
Honey, why do you think
we stayed put here all these years?

121
00:08:49.780 --> 00:08:53.610
Because we believed one day
you'd find us again.

122
00:08:53.742 --> 00:08:54.912
Exactly!

123
00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:58.579
But I thought you were gone.
How did you...

124
00:08:58.664 --> 00:09:01.714
We went into quarantine
to look for you, but you weren't there.

125
00:09:01.875 --> 00:09:04.875
And we knew you must have
gotten out through the pipes.

126
00:09:05.045 --> 00:09:07.399
Through the pipes. That's right, sweetie.
And so we did too.

127
00:09:07.423 --> 00:09:11.263
And we've stayed in this spot for you
ever since.

128
00:09:11.427 --> 00:09:13.905
- We thought you might come back.
- We stayed and waited for you.

129
00:09:13.929 --> 00:09:16.929
So every day, we go out and lay out...

130
00:09:17.891 --> 00:09:18.971
Shells.

131
00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:29.270
And you found us.
Oh honey, you found us.

132
00:09:29.445 --> 00:09:31.945
And you know why you found us?
Because you remembered.

133
00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:38.410
You remembered
in your own, amazing, Dory way.

134
00:09:40.914 --> 00:09:43.794
I did. All by myself.

135
00:09:43.959 --> 00:09:49.459
Oh, honey. Really? Have you been
by yourself all these years?

136
00:09:49.631 --> 00:09:51.301
Oh, my poor little girl.

137
00:09:51.467 --> 00:09:55.137
Oh, I haven't been all by myself...
Marlin and Nemo!

138
00:09:56.263 --> 00:09:58.575
- Nobody saw where Dory went?
- No. Sorry. I didn't see anything.

139
00:09:58.599 --> 00:10:01.509
Seriously? That's a lot
of eyeballs doing nothing.

140
00:10:01.769 --> 00:10:03.349
Oh! Oh, excuse me. Can you help us?

141
00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:05.020
- We're looking...
- Me help you?

142
00:10:08.817 --> 00:10:10.657
Dad, look! It's Dory.

143
00:10:10.778 --> 00:10:15.248
Oh, thank goodness. See, Nemo,
I knew she'd find a way... What?

144
00:10:15.366 --> 00:10:16.786
Hey, where's Dory? Is she with you?

145
00:10:16.867 --> 00:10:18.957
I'm sorry.

146
00:10:19.036 --> 00:10:21.996
I tried to hold on,
but I couldn't and I lost her.

147
00:10:22.122 --> 00:10:24.082
- What?
- All right. Let's get going.

148
00:10:24.208 --> 00:10:25.378
No!

149
00:10:25.542 --> 00:10:28.062
And then the whale swallowed us
even though I speak whale.

150
00:10:28.128 --> 00:10:29.128
A whale?

151
00:10:29.171 --> 00:10:30.357
Good thing I wasn't
there to see that.

152
00:10:30.381 --> 00:10:32.442
Actually Marlin never believes
I even know how to speak whale...

153
00:10:32.466 --> 00:10:34.486
but you know what, he always kind of
trusts me anyway.

154
00:10:34.510 --> 00:10:36.010
You know, I like this Marlin already.

155
00:10:36.178 --> 00:10:38.648
Yeah. And then somehow
we found Nemo. Or did he find me?

156
00:10:38.806 --> 00:10:41.226
I don't know. But, you know what,
Nemo is the sweetest.

157
00:10:41.392 --> 00:10:43.112
He just never gives up on me
no matter what.

158
00:10:43.185 --> 00:10:44.355
Um, what would Dory do?

159
00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:47.310
Well, we'll certainly have to thank
Marlin and Nemo when we meet them.

160
00:10:48.857 --> 00:10:51.027
Wait. Wait I know this place.

161
00:10:51.235 --> 00:10:54.235
Hello. I'm Sigourney Weaver.

162
00:10:54.363 --> 00:10:56.153
- There!
- Won't you please join us?

163
00:10:57.074 --> 00:11:00.204
- That's the Marine Life Institute.
- Oh, you were born there.

164
00:11:00.369 --> 00:11:01.199
Dory, is that where your friends are?

165
00:11:01.370 --> 00:11:05.410
Yes! They were stuck in something.
It was going somewhere.

166
00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:08.468
A truck. They're in the truck!

167
00:11:08.544 --> 00:11:10.544
That means I could...
Never see them again!

168
00:11:10.712 --> 00:11:12.752
No! No, no, no. What would Dory do?

169
00:11:13.715 --> 00:11:17.885
Uh, I know they're good friends of yours,
but a truck is kind of a tall order.

170
00:11:18.971 --> 00:11:21.221
Please! Please.
All I know is that I miss them. I... I...

171
00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:26.220
I really miss them.
I've said that before.

172
00:11:27.729 --> 00:11:28.729
Um...

173
00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:29.896
Dory?

174
00:11:30.023 --> 00:11:34.733
Mom, Marlin and Nemo are more
than good friends, they're family.

175
00:11:34.903 --> 00:11:38.783
And I have to get them back.
See, when they found me it felt like fate.

176
00:11:38.907 --> 00:11:41.707
Do you know what I mean? Or... I don't...
What's another word for fate?

177
00:11:41.743 --> 00:11:44.833
Like destiny. Destiny?

178
00:11:44.913 --> 00:11:46.623
Destiny!

179
00:11:47.124 --> 00:11:49.044
- Dory?
- Destiny!

180
00:11:49.209 --> 00:11:52.459
- Morning, Dest...
- Sh. It's Dory. Something's wrong.

181
00:11:54.256 --> 00:11:57.596
Ooh. I got her.
She's right outside the institute.

182
00:11:59.386 --> 00:12:00.697
- Destiny?
- We got to jump.

183
00:12:00.721 --> 00:12:02.301
- Jump?
- No time to argue!

184
00:12:02.431 --> 00:12:03.931
Destiny!

185
00:12:04.057 --> 00:12:06.937
Dory! The truck thing
with your friends is leaving!

186
00:12:07.102 --> 00:12:08.892
No, no. Destiny.

187
00:12:08.979 --> 00:12:11.229
Oh no! That's bad!
What do we do?

188
00:12:13.692 --> 00:12:14.772
- All right.
- Yes.

189
00:12:14.943 --> 00:12:17.443
- Here we go. One. Two.
- Yes. Yes.

190
00:12:17.571 --> 00:12:19.651
I can't! I can't do it!
I'll never make it out there.

191
00:12:19.698 --> 00:12:23.118
Destiny! I've got the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

192
00:12:23.285 --> 00:12:25.096
You've got the world's
most powerful pair of glasses.

193
00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:26.450
I will be your eyes.

194
00:12:26.622 --> 00:12:28.952
You can be my eyes. But the walls!

195
00:12:29.082 --> 00:12:31.162
There are no walls in the ocean!

196
00:12:31.793 --> 00:12:34.923
- No walls?
- It's your destiny, Destiny.

197
00:12:35.047 --> 00:12:37.097
Well, why didn't you say so?

198
00:12:37.257 --> 00:12:40.597
What? No! Destiny, wait!
No, that's a wall! Wall!

199
00:12:45.974 --> 00:12:48.684
Mom, Dad, this is my pipe pal.
Destiny, say hi.

200
00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:50.732
Dory! Are these little blue blobs
your parents?

201
00:12:50.812 --> 00:12:52.192
They look just like you!

202
00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:55.486
Hello. I'm Bailey. Mrs. Dory, Mr. Dory.

203
00:12:55.651 --> 00:12:57.170
- Oh please, call me Jenny.
- Oh and I'm Charlie.

204
00:12:57.194 --> 00:12:59.234
Okay. Okay. We got to go.
We got to stop that truck.

205
00:12:59.655 --> 00:13:00.655
Okay, what truck?

206
00:13:03.325 --> 00:13:04.665
Bailey, status report.

207
00:13:04.826 --> 00:13:07.996
Oh, yes, my beautiful gift. Ooh.

208
00:13:08.163 --> 00:13:10.333
Found it! The truck's merging
onto the freeway

209
00:13:10.415 --> 00:13:11.835
and it's heading south. Ooh.

210
00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.290
Let's go. We are stopping that truck.

211
00:13:15.712 --> 00:13:18.462
- This I've got to see.
- Yeah, yeah, me too!

212
00:13:19.174 --> 00:13:21.594
Oh boy, this is gonna be good!

213
00:13:21.677 --> 00:13:24.137
What the... Gerald!
Have you lost your marbles?

214
00:13:24.304 --> 00:13:26.804
- Don't get used to it, Gerald!
- Cheeky joke.

215
00:13:30.018 --> 00:13:31.898
Bailey, I forgot everything.
Catch me up.

216
00:13:32.062 --> 00:13:35.022
Yes, ma'am. Ooh.
Your friends are still on the truck.

217
00:13:35.190 --> 00:13:37.730
Ooh. They're headed north
towards the bridge. Ooh.

218
00:13:37.901 --> 00:13:40.231
Oh, look, there's a bunch of
cute otters over there.

219
00:13:40.362 --> 00:13:41.782
I want one! Ow!

220
00:13:45.117 --> 00:13:46.577
Ow, Bailey!

221
00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.740
Oh! I see the truck. It's over there.

222
00:13:48.912 --> 00:13:50.723
- Okay, what would Dory do?
- I don't see how we can get on it.

223
00:13:50.747 --> 00:13:52.757
Oh, man, if only there was a way
to stop traffic.

224
00:13:52.916 --> 00:13:55.506
Stop traffic. Stop traffic!
Everyone needs to stop.

225
00:13:55.669 --> 00:13:56.688
People stop to look at things.

226
00:13:56.712 --> 00:13:58.314
Things that they like.
Things that are cute.

227
00:13:58.338 --> 00:14:01.308
Things that are cute!
Okay, I got it.

228
00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:03.183
- What? What is it?
- Quickly before I forget.

229
00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:05.880
Destiny, when the truck reaches
the bridge you flip me up there.

230
00:14:06.054 --> 00:14:06.634
Got it.

231
00:14:06.763 --> 00:14:09.553
You guys, follow me.
Everyone else, stay here.

232
00:14:09.725 --> 00:14:13.275
Whoa. Dory.
Honey, you're not leaving us again.

233
00:14:13.437 --> 00:14:15.237
Your mother's right.
You have to stay with us.

234
00:14:15.272 --> 00:14:19.112
Dory, what happens if...
You know, if you're gone for too long.

235
00:14:19.276 --> 00:14:22.088
And what if you get confused and that
makes you distracted. And what if...

236
00:14:22.112 --> 00:14:23.402
I lose you again?

237
00:14:24.281 --> 00:14:26.031
Oh. Yes.

238
00:14:27.492 --> 00:14:30.282
Mom, Dad,
it's gonna be okay because...

239
00:14:30.454 --> 00:14:34.254
I know that even if I forget
I can find you again.

240
